<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Euboeote Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1256">1256</a>–<a href="/years/1258">1258</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Euboeote Succession was fought from 1256 to 1258 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-villehardouin">William II of Villehardouin</a>, prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, and a coalition of the lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Euboea</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-i-de-la-roche">Guy I de la Roche</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, over the succession to a lordship in Euboea. William's victory at Karydi in 1258 confirmed his supremacy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-euboeote-succession.jpg" alt="War of the Euboeote Succession" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William R. Shepherd · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ShepherdByzempire1265.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
